diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..d1b9c1d 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,6 +2,10 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+Each subscribed board event creates one delivery and one `POST` to the payload URL. Failed deliveries are logged but are not retried. The request body is JSON and the `X-Webhook-Signature` header is the hexadecimal HMAC-SHA256 of the exact request body, using the webhook's `signing_secret`. `X-Webhook-Timestamp` contains the event timestamp.
+
+A successful delivery resets the webhook's failure streak. A webhook is automatically deactivated after at least ten consecutive failures spanning one hour, and can be reactivated through the activation endpoint. Delivery history is retained for one week.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks`
 
 Returns a paginated list of webhooks for a board.
